{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-83615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the distance between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-83615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2-2)^{2}+(3-0)^{2}+(5-5)^{2}+(4-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+9+0+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-83615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "159578338113af9e880a73a2290c85b1f474b881efbb78f5a2c6b4f033834018"} {"question" "q-83615" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-83615" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-83615" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-83617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the distance between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-83617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3-2)^{2}+(-3-(-1))^{2}+(0-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-83617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "159578338113af9e880a73a2290c85b1f474b881efbb78f5a2c6b4f033834018"} {"question" "q-83617" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-83617" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"] ["text" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-83617" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-86822" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the distance between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-86822" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0-1)^{2}+(0-(-1))^{2}+(3-2)^{2}+(1-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-86822" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "159578338113af9e880a73a2290c85b1f474b881efbb78f5a2c6b4f033834018"} {"question" "q-86822" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-86822" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-86822" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-139468" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the distance between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-139468" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-17 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-17 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(5-3)^{2}+(5-6)^{2}+(1-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-139468" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "159578338113af9e880a73a2290c85b1f474b881efbb78f5a2c6b4f033834018"} {"question" "q-139468" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-139468" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-139468" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-39866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the distance between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-39866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 22\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -16\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}22 & -8 \\\\ -8 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -16\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3-2)^{2}+(2-2)^{2}+(1-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-39866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "159578338113af9e880a73a2290c85b1f474b881efbb78f5a2c6b4f033834018"} {"question" "q-39866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-39866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-39866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-139513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the acute angle between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRound the answer to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-139513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}11 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 8\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{24}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -8 \\\\ -8 & 11\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ Equivalently, it is the acute angle between $x$ and any non-zero vector that is parallel to ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ So, to make calculations easier, we can find the angle between the vectors\n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,2\\,{\\text{proj}}_{S}x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{x\\cdot {\\text{proj}}_{S}x}{‖x‖‖{\\text{proj}}_{S}x‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{9}\\sqrt{30}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{3\\sqrt{30}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}})≈{24.09}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-139513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "159578338113af9e880a73a2290c85b1f474b881efbb78f5a2c6b4f033834018"} {"question" "q-139513" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-139513" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{19.24}^{∘}"] ["math" "{22.73}^{∘}"] ["math" "{24.09}^{∘}"] ["math" "{24.11}^{∘}"] ["math" "{27.53}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-139513" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{24.09}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-139477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the acute angle between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-139477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ Equivalently, it is the acute angle between $x$ and any non-zero vector that is parallel to ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ So, to make calculations easier, we can find the angle between the vectors\n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,2\\,{\\text{proj}}_{S}x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1}\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{4},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-139477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "159578338113af9e880a73a2290c85b1f474b881efbb78f5a2c6b4f033834018"} {"question" "q-139477" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-139477" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-139477" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-139478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the acute angle between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-139478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 27\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}27 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ Equivalently, it is the acute angle between $x$ and any non-zero vector that is parallel to ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ So, to make calculations easier, we can find the angle between the vectors\n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,2\\,{\\text{proj}}_{S}x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{(-6)\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 6}{\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{\\sqrt{54}\\sqrt{54}} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{54} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{3},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-139478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "159578338113af9e880a73a2290c85b1f474b881efbb78f5a2c6b4f033834018"} {"question" "q-139478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-139478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-139478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-86829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the acute angle between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRound the answer to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-86829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ Equivalently, it is the acute angle between $x$ and any non-zero vector that is parallel to ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ So, to make calculations easier, we can find the angle between the vectors\n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,3\\,{\\text{proj}}_{S}x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (-4)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{3}\\sqrt{24}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{3}\\sqrt{3\\cdot 8}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{3})≈{19.47}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-86829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "159578338113af9e880a73a2290c85b1f474b881efbb78f5a2c6b4f033834018"} {"question" "q-86829" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-86829" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{19.47}^{∘}"] ["math" "{21}^{∘}"] ["math" "{32.54}^{∘}"] ["math" "{37}^{∘}"] ["math" "{45.77}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-86829" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{19.47}^{∘}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-39877" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the acute angle between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRound the answer to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-39877" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 9\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$   \n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{x\\cdot {\\text{proj}}_{S}x}{‖x‖‖{\\text{proj}}_{S}x‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{14}\\sqrt{12}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{2\\sqrt{42}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{42}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{42}})≈{22.21}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-39877" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "159578338113af9e880a73a2290c85b1f474b881efbb78f5a2c6b4f033834018"} {"question" "q-39877" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-39877" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{14.21}^{∘}"] ["math" "{22.21}^{∘}"] ["math" "{34.05}^{∘}"] ["math" "{45.12}^{∘}"] ["math" "{54.05}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-39877" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{22.21}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-81435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-4{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-81435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to its row echelon form. Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}$ are free variables. Now, from the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}={x}_{3}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is the basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nNow, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-81435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "159578338113af9e880a73a2290c85b1f474b881efbb78f5a2c6b4f033834018"} {"question" "q-81435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-81435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-81435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-40619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-40619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find a basis for the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}$ are free variables. Now, from the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{3}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is the basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nNow, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-40619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "159578338113af9e880a73a2290c85b1f474b881efbb78f5a2c6b4f033834018"} {"question" "q-40619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-40619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-40619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-39858" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-9{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-39858" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find a basis for the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -9 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}$ are free variables. Now, from the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is the basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nNow, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}10 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-39858" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "159578338113af9e880a73a2290c85b1f474b881efbb78f5a2c6b4f033834018"} {"question" "q-39858" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070757/state.json" "file_sha256" "13b365e05a449e36435067efbdfb2b40b798a38e1ab0edec6a3f64d447d70bd1"} {"question" "q-39858" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6 